 "text": "Hey there, how are you? The short bottle wraps in ice cubes. Use a lid that holds ice and keeps the bottle upright, and lots of ice in the bottle itself. Keep it right by the ice in the container. A bottle of red can heat up fast in the sun, so keep it in the shade. I' used it for years. The key is keeping the bottle in the shade and the ice from melting. Keep them under an umbrella and keep the ice in them from melting. A frozen water bottle in the freezer keeps the drinks cold for hours.",
